   "date": "2013-12-02",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The speaker moved the Customs Tariff Amendment (Carbon Tax Repeal) Bill 2013 to remove carbon tax elements from the Customs Tariff Act, arguing it would reduce excise-equivalent customs duty on aviation fuel and citing Qantas surcharges of $1.93–$7.25 per passenger and similar Virgin Australia surcharges, with the repeal expected to lower airline costs and enable savings for travellers."
